#, no-c-format
msgid "W*"
msgstr "W* - W*"

#, no-c-format
msgid "Average dry thermal updraft strength near mid-BL height. Subtract glider descent rate to get average vario reading for cloudless thermals. Updraft strengths will be stronger than this forecast if convective clouds are present, since cloud condensation adds buoyancy aloft (i.e. this neglects \"cloudsuck\"). W* depends upon both the surface heating and the BL depth."
msgstr "Prosek sešliščni tekmilski pohod v sredini visine BL. Odštejite spustajočo hitrost letala, da dobite prosek četrtnečnikov mnenje za neoblačne termike. Pohodna hitrost bo večja, če so prisotni konvektivni oblaki, ker se v nih zvratno teče vzhod (tj. to zanemari \"oblakosuck\"). W* odvisni je od obeh poverilnikov podnevanja in dubine BL."

#, no-c-format
msgid "BL Wind spd"
msgstr "BL Vjeterni hitrost"

#, no-c-format
msgid "The speed and direction of the vector-averaged wind in the BL. This prediction can be misleading if there is a large change in wind direction through the BL."
msgstr "Hitrost in smer vektorsko povprečenega vjetra v BL. Ta predviđanje lahko zaviri, če postanejo velike spremembe v smeri vjetra skozi BL."

#, no-c-format
msgid "H bl"
msgstr "H bl - V bl"

#, no-c-format
msgid "Height of the top of the mixing layer, which for thermal convection is the average top of a dry thermal. Over flat terrain, maximum thermalling heights will be lower due to the glider descent rate and other factors. In the presence of clouds (which release additional buoyancy aloft, creating \"cloudsuck\") the updraft top will be above this forecast, but the maximum thermalling height will then be limited by the cloud base. Further, when the mixing results from shear turbulence rather than thermal mixing this parameter is not useful for glider flying."
msgstr "Višina vrha smijevega sloja, ki je za termično konvekcijo povprečna vrh sešliščnega tekmila. Na ravni terene bo maksimalna visina tekmiljanja manjša zaradi spustajoče hitrosti letala in drugih faktorov. V prisotnosti oblakov (ki vložijo dodatno zvratno tečnost vzhod, ustvarjujo \"oblakosuck\"), vrh sešliščnega pohoda bo višji od toga predviđanja, vendar maksimalna visina tekmiljanja bo omejena s podzemljem oblaka. Dopolnilno pa je, če je smijevega sloja rezultat razmerje vzhodnega vjetra, ta parametar za letanje sešlišča ni uporaben."

#, no-c-format
msgid "dwcrit"
msgstr "dwcrit - dolžina kritične termike"

#, no-c-format
msgid "bl cloud"
msgstr "bl oblaki"

#, no-c-format
msgid "This parameter provides an additional means of evaluating the formation of clouds within the BL and might be used either in conjunction with or instead of the other cloud prediction parameters. It assumes a very simple relationship between cloud cover percentage and the maximum relative humidity within the BL. The cloud base height is not predicted, but is expected to be below the BL Top height."
msgstr "Ta parametar ponuja dodatno način ocene formiranja oblakov v BL in se lahko uporablja either splošne ali namreč kot alternativa drugim predviđanjem o oblakih. Predpostavlja zelo preprosto odnos med procento pokritosti oblaka in maksimalno relativno vlhkost v BL. Višina podzemlja oblaka ni predviđana, ampak je očitna, da bo manjša kot višina vrha BL."

#, no-c-format
msgid "Sfc temp"
msgstr "Površinska temperatura"

#, no-c-format
msgid "The temperature at a height of 2m above ground level. This can be compared to observed surface temperatures as an indication of model simulation accuracy; e.g. if observed surface temperatures are significantly below those forecast, then soaring conditions will be poorer than forecast."
msgstr "Temperatura na višini 2m nad površino. To se lahko primerja z pomerenimi površinskimi temperaturemi kot oznako za točnost modelnega simulacije; npr., če so pomereni površinske temperature znatno nižje, od predviđanj, bodo letanje kondicije slabše."

